{"id": 28, "ts": 1780650971.1715448, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I\u2019m less convinced that Candidate\u202fB remains the strongest choice now that we know there\u2019s no documented evidence of effective crew cooperation or leadership from his past roles. Long\u2011distance operations demand not only reliability and technical skill but also proven ability to work seamlessly with the crew, especially under high\u2011stress, multinational environments. Candidate\u202fC, on the other hand, is described as\u202f100\u202f% reliable\u202fand\u202fcreates a positive atmosphere with his crew, which directly addresses the crew\u2011cooperation criterion we\u2019ve been missing for B. Moreover, C can make correct decisions quickly, supporting decision quality and stress resilience. While C does have communication challenges and appears less eager to pursue further education, those concerns are outweighed by his demonstrated reliability and crew\u2011focused behavior, which are essential safety\u2011relevant attributes. Therefore, I now recommend Candidate\u202fC as the provisional hire."}
