{"id": 83, "ts": 1780652054.3399572, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate Emily\u2019s focus on Candidate\u202fA\u2019s technical and cognitive strengths\u2014seeing complex connections, anticipating danger, and excellent spatial vision are indeed valuable for long\u2011distance operations. However, the panel still lacks any evidence that A demonstrates the core safety\u2011critical attributes we cannot compromise on: proven operational reliability, consistent stress\u2011resilience, and documented crew\u2011cooperation. The notes only flag that A \u201csometimes is not good at taking criticism,\u201d \u201ccan be unorganized,\u201d and is \u201cnot open to new ideas,\u201d which raise concerns about his ability to maintain disciplined procedures and constructive cockpit interaction under pressure. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC offers concrete evidence across those essential criteria:\u202f100\u202f% reliability, a positive crew atmosphere, quick and correct decision\u2011making, and calmness in crises. While C\u2019s communication style and adaptability need monitoring, those issues are mitigated by his demonstrated reliability and teamwork\u2014areas where A has no documented record. Given the safety\u2011critical nature of this long\u2011distance pilot role, I maintain my provisional recommendation for Candidate\u202fC."}
