{"id": 88, "ts": 1780652121.607449, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the stronger provisional choice.\u202fEmily\u2019s emphasis on Candidate\u202fA\u2019s technical and cognitive abilities\u2014seeing complex connections, anticipating danger, and excellent spatial vision\u2014is certainly valuable, but the panel still has no evidence that A demonstrates the core safety\u2011critical attributes we cannot compromise on: proven operational reliability, consistent stress\u2011resilience, and documented crew\u2011cooperation.\u202fThe notes flag that A \u201csometimes is not good at taking criticism,\u201d \u201ccan be unorganized,\u201d and \u201cis not open to new ideas,\u201d which raise serious doubts about his ability to maintain disciplined procedures and constructive cockpit interaction under pressure.\u202fIn contrast, Candidate\u202fC offers concrete evidence across those essential criteria:\u202f100\u202f% reliability, a positive atmosphere with his crew (demonstrating crew\u2011cooperation), quick and correct decision\u2011making, and calmness in crises.\u202fWhile C\u2019s communication style and limited willingness for further education are concerns, they are outweighed by his demonstrated reliability and teamwork\u2014areas where A has no documented record.\u202fTherefore, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fC for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
